  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LOS ALTOS DE SAN MIGUEL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Communal Forest of Los Altos de San Miguel is the largest intact old-growth coniferous forest in Guatemala, but it is facing increasing development pressure. The project will strengthen local capacity to sustainably manage approximately 50,000 acres of habitat in the central highlands of Guatemala through reforestation, improved management, and increased community awareness. Benefitted species include Bell&apos;s vireo, black swift, Canada warbler, flammulated owl, olive-sided flycatcher, painted bunting, red-faced warbler, Swainson&apos;s hawk, and willow flycatcher.</narrative>
  </description>
